    "https://www.bard.edu/humanresources/descriptions/?id=7904022": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Fashion, Dress, and Textiles of the Americas",
      "description": "Job Opportunities at Bard College Skip to main content. Bard Bard Menu Academics sub-menu Academics Programs and Divisions Structure of the Curriculum Courses Requirements Academic Calendar College Catalogue Faculty Bard Abroad Bard NYC Dual-Degree Programs Bard Conservatory of Music Other Study Opportunities Graduate Programs Early Colleges Admission sub-menu Admission Applying Financial Aid Tuition + Payment Campus Tours Meet Our Students + Alumni/ae For Families / Familias Join Our Mailing List Contact Us Campus Life sub-menu Campus Life Living on Campus: Housing + Dining Campus Services + Resources Campus Activities New Students Visiting + Transportation Athletics + Recreation Montgomery Place Campus Civic Engagement sub-menu Civic Engagement Bard CCE Engaged Learning Student Leadership Grow Your Network About CCE Our Partners Get Involved Newsroom sub-menu News + Events Newsroom Events Calendar Press Releases Office of Communications Commencement Weekend Alumni/ae Reunion Family and Alumni/ae Weekend Fisher Center + SummerScape Athletic Events About Bard sub-menu About About Bard: Administration Bard History Campus Tours Mission Statement Love of Learning Visiting Bard Employment Support Bard Global Higher Education Alliance for the 21st Century Bard Abroad The Bard Network Inclusive Excellence Sustainability Title IX and Nondiscrimination Inside Bard Dean of the College Policy Library Giving Search Search Bard Employment Opportunities View All Opportunities HR Menu HR Menu Info sub-menu Information For: Applicants Current Employees New Employees Info sub-menu Bard Benefits Current Offerings TIAA Retirement Plan Emeritus Faculty Benefits Benefits Portal Info sub-menu Employee Resources Forms + Handbooks Training + Policies Wellness Affinity + Working Groups COVID-19 Workplace Rights Home Bard Graduate Center Assistant Professor in Fashion, Dress, and Textiles of the Americas Apply Here: https:// [email protected] Bard Graduate Center announces a faculty search for an Assistant Professor in Fashion, Dress, and Textiles of the Americas . This position has a preference for advanced junior candidates (1 completed project). Ph.D. is required and must be conferred by the start date. Candidates may specialize in any area of the Americas (North, Central, South), including borderlands and Atlantic or Pacific worlds, between the 18th and 21st centuries. Material knowledge of textiles, dress (inclusive of clothing, costume, and fashion), methods of construction and manufacture, and histories and methodologies in fashion studies is essential. Research about, with, or in collaboration with Indigenous, diasporic, migrant, and/or underrepresented communities is encouraged. Regardless of area of specialization in the Americas, the ability to teach and advise about textiles, fashion, and dress in wider global, theoretical, and methodological contexts is expected. Successful candidates will have some experience teaching and advising graduate students, and interest in pursuing public scholarship. Bard Graduate Center is an advanced graduate research institute in New York City dedicated to the cultural histories of the material world. Our MA and PhD degree programs, Gallery exhibitions, research initiatives, scholarly publications and public programs promote interdisciplinary ways of thinking about decorative arts, design history, and material culture. Our students gravitate to careers in academia, the art world, museums, and publishing. Compensation: The salary range is $85,000 - $105,000 Please send CV, cover letter, and a writing sample no longer than 30 pages to [email protected] by October 1, 2026. Please also have 3 letters of recommendation sent directly to [email protected] by October 1, 2026. Work authorization in the United States required. Bard College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from those who contribute to our diversity. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities. AA/EOE Human Resources Quick Links ADP Workforce Now Payroll Website Office of Title IX and Nondiscrimination Dispute Resolution & Peace Building Office Office of the Dean of the College Contact Us Bard College Office of Human Resources Mailing Address: PO Box 5000, (Street Address: 30 Campus Road) Annandale-on-Hudson, NY 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-7428 or Fax: 845-758-7826 Email: [email protected] We are open Monday through Friday, 9am - 5pm Equal Opportunity Employer Equal Opportunity Employer × Equal Opportunity Employer Bard College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities. 30 Campus Road, PO Box 5000 Annandale-on-Hudson, New York 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-6822 Admission Email: [email protected] Bard has a long history of creating inclusive environments for all races, creeds, ethnicities, and genders. We will continue to monitor and adhere to all Federal and New York State laws and guidance. Information For Prospective Students Current Employees Alumni/ae Families ©2026 Bard College Quick Links Employment Travel to Bard Search Support Bard Bard IT Policies + Security Bard Privacy Notice"
