    "https://www.bard.edu/humanresources/descriptions/?id=3966076": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Representative",
      "description": "Job Opportunities at Bard College Skip to main content. Bard Bard Menu Academics sub-menu Academics Programs and Divisions Structure of the Curriculum Courses Requirements Academic Calendar College Catalogue Faculty Bard Abroad Bard NYC Dual-Degree Programs Bard Conservatory of Music Other Study Opportunities Graduate Programs Early Colleges Admission sub-menu Admission Applying Financial Aid Tuition + Payment Campus Tours Meet Our Students + Alumni/ae For Families / Familias Join Our Mailing List Contact Us Campus Life sub-menu Campus Life Living on Campus: Housing + Dining Campus Services + Resources Campus Activities New Students Visiting + Transportation Athletics + Recreation Montgomery Place Campus Civic Engagement sub-menu Civic Engagement Bard CCE Engaged Learning Student Leadership Grow Your Network About CCE Our Partners Get Involved Newsroom sub-menu News + Events Newsroom Events Calendar Press Releases Office of Communications Commencement Weekend Alumni/ae Reunion Family and Alumni/ae Weekend Fisher Center + SummerScape Athletic Events About Bard sub-menu About About Bard: Administration Bard History Campus Tours Mission Statement Love of Learning Visiting Bard Employment Support Bard Global Higher Education Alliance for the 21st Century Bard Abroad The Bard Network Inclusive Excellence Sustainability Title IX and Nondiscrimination Inside Bard Dean of the College Policy Library Giving Search Search Bard Employment Opportunities View All Opportunities HR Menu HR Menu Info sub-menu Information For: Applicants Current Employees New Employees Info sub-menu Bard Benefits Current Offerings TIAA Retirement Plan Emeritus Faculty Benefits Benefits Portal Info sub-menu Employee Resources Forms + Handbooks Training + Policies Wellness Affinity + Working Groups COVID-19 Workplace Rights Home Bard College Student Accounts Representative Apply Here: https://apply.interfolio.com/192380 Bard College seeks a Student Accounts Representative to join the Student Financial Services (SFS) department. The Student Accounts Representative is a full-time position responsible for the day-to-day student account functions and will report directly to the Director of Student Financial Services. The successful candidate will have a high level of professionalism and confidence in customer service and be able to handle confidential student information. It is critical that the individual in this role bring strong verbal and written communication skills and attention to detail. They must also have the ability to multi-task and prioritize duties in a fast-paced, ever-changing environment. The successful candidate will excel at working in an environment that is broadly diverse with regard to race, ethnicity, socioeconomic status, gender, nationality, sexual orientation, and religion. This is a full-time, year-round, benefits-eligible position located on the Annandale campus of Bard College. The position requires availability to work occasional weekends and evenings, as needed. About Bard: Bard College’s main campus is in Annandale-on-Hudson, N.Y., with 1,900 undergraduate students; the College also includes multiple graduate programs. The 1,000-acre campus sits along the Hudson River and offers the Fisher Performing Arts Center, and Hessel Museum of Art, and is the home of the Bard Prison Initiative, the largest college-degree-granting prison education program in the U.S. The Bard Network also includes several Bard High School Early Colleges across the country as well as international campuses and partnerships. Bard College is a private institution working in the public interest. Bard faculty and staff lead their students by example, building upon the existing network of boundary-breaking programs focused on rethinking who can and should be included in a liberal arts education. Responsibilities: Assist with inquiries in person, on the phone, and via email regarding current and delinquent student account balances, payment deadlines, status of refund checks, and other student account related inquiries Assist students and parents in making payments, setting up a payment plan, waiving optional charges, and adding money to their flex accounts Process, review, print and mail monthly billing statements Review refund requests Assist with 1098-T tax form inquires Assist with the daily processing of payments to students accounts via cash, check and wire transfers Maintain in-depth knowledge of the college's policies and procedures in regards to billing and refund policies, institutional and FERPA confidentiality regulations Maintain a general knowledge of Financial Aid information to assist students and families in a holistic way Serve as the back-up for other Student Financial Aid Services functions Protect the confidentiality of student records and files within Student Financial Services Apply College policies and procedures and federal and/or state laws and regulations regarding financial aid and cash management functions and confidentiality regulations as needed Other special projects and job-related duties as assigned Qualifications: Prior customer service experience required; higher education experience preferred Associate’s degree preferred Competency in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Knowledge of Ellucian Banner a plus Excellent verbal and written communication skills Organization, accuracy and keen attention to detail Ability to work with confidential information Must be able to work occasional weekends and evenings, as needed Must be able to occasionally lift 20 pounds To Apply: Please provide a cover letter, resume, and the contact information for three professional references to Interfolio by following this link: https://apply.interfolio.com/192380 . Compensation: $26 - $28 per hour This salary range reflects the College's good faith and reasonable estimate of the compensation for the position at the time of the job posting. Salary decisions are dependent on several factors including but not limited to market and organizational considerations, experience, and qualifications of a selected candidate as well as internal and external equity. Benefits Overview: We are pleased to offer our full-time employees an excellent benefit package which includes multiple health insurance options; TIAA retirement plans; generous vacation, sick, and personal time; and more. To learn more about employee benefits and eligibility at Bard College, please visit https://www.bard.edu/humanresources/benefits/ . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Bard is an equal-opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from those who contribute to our diversity. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities. AA/EOE Human Resources Quick Links ADP Workforce Now Payroll Website Office of Title IX and Nondiscrimination Dispute Resolution & Peace Building Office Office of the Dean of the College Contact Us Bard College Office of Human Resources Mailing Address: PO Box 5000, (Street Address: 30 Campus Road) Annandale-on-Hudson, NY 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-7428 or Fax: 845-758-7826 Email: hr@bard.edu We are open Monday through Friday, 9am - 5pm Equal Opportunity Employer Equal Opportunity Employer 30 Campus Road, PO Box 5000 Annandale-on-Hudson, New York 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-6822 Admission Email: admission@bard.edu Bard has a long history of creating inclusive environments for all races, creeds, ethnicities, and genders. We will continue to monitor and adhere to all Federal and New York State laws and guidance. Information For Prospective Students Current Employees Alumni/ae Families ©2026 Bard College Quick Links Employment Travel to Bard Search Support Bard Bard IT Policies + Security Bard Privacy Notice × Equal Opportunity Employer Bard College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities."
