    "https://www.bard.edu/humanresources/descriptions/?id=4064416": {
      "title": "Admissions Support Assistant (short-term)",
      "description": "Job Opportunities at Bard College Skip to main content. Bard Bard Menu Academics sub-menu Academics Programs and Divisions Structure of the Curriculum Courses Requirements Academic Calendar College Catalogue Faculty Bard Abroad Bard NYC Dual-Degree Programs Bard Conservatory of Music Other Study Opportunities Graduate Programs Early Colleges Admission sub-menu Admission Applying Financial Aid Tuition + Payment Campus Tours Meet Our Students + Alumni/ae For Families / Familias Join Our Mailing List Contact Us Campus Life sub-menu Campus Life Living on Campus: Housing + Dining Campus Services + Resources Campus Activities New Students Visiting + Transportation Athletics + Recreation Montgomery Place Campus Civic Engagement sub-menu Civic Engagement Bard CCE Engaged Learning Student Leadership Grow Your Network About CCE Our Partners Get Involved Newsroom sub-menu News + Events Newsroom Events Calendar Press Releases Office of Communications Commencement Weekend Alumni/ae Reunion Family and Alumni/ae Weekend Fisher Center + SummerScape Athletic Events About Bard sub-menu About About Bard: Administration Bard History Campus Tours Mission Statement Love of Learning Visiting Bard Employment Support Bard Global Higher Education Alliance for the 21st Century Bard Abroad The Bard Network Inclusive Excellence Sustainability Title IX and Nondiscrimination Inside Bard Dean of the College Policy Library Giving Search Search Bard Employment Opportunities View All Opportunities HR Menu HR Menu Info sub-menu Information For: Applicants Current Employees New Employees Info sub-menu Bard Benefits Current Offerings TIAA Retirement Plan Emeritus Faculty Benefits Benefits Portal Info sub-menu Employee Resources Forms + Handbooks Training + Policies Wellness Affinity + Working Groups COVID-19 Workplace Rights Home Bard High School Early College Brooklyn Admissions Support Assistant (short-term) Apply Here: https://apply.interfolio.com/195852 About the Bard High School Early Colleges Bard Early Colleges (BECs) are founded on the belief that many high school–age students are eager and ready for the intellectual challenges of a college education. Bard Early Colleges act on this belief by providing younger scholars with a tuition-free, credit-bearing college course of study in the liberal arts and sciences following the 9th and 10th grades. Students are taught by college faculty and have the opportunity to earn up to 60 college credits and an associate in arts (A.A.) degree from Bard College, concurrently with a high school diploma. Bard Early Colleges begin preparing students for college work as early as the 9th grade and offer ongoing guidance and academic support. Now in its third decade, the Bard Early College network serves over 3,300 students in campuses in The Bronx, Lower Manhattan, Queens, Brooklyn, and Hudson, New York; Newark, New Jersey; New Orleans, Louisiana; Cleveland, Ohio; Washington, D.C.; and Baltimore, Maryland. Since 2003, Bard College has awarded more than 5,500 A.A. degrees to its early college students. About Bard High School Early College Brooklyn Campus Launched in 2024, Bard High School Early College Brooklyn (BHSEC Brooklyn) is a new and innovative public early college high school in the East New York neighborhood of Brooklyn. BHSEC seeks to provide a rigorous course of study that emphasizes thinking through writing, discussion, and inquiry. This alternative to the traditional high school is founded on the belief that many young people are ready and eager to do serious college work at age sixteen. Based on the premise that these young adults' ambition to learn must be taken seriously, BHSEC's four-year program enables highly motivated students to earn a New York State high school Regents diploma and a tuition-free Bard College associate's degree in four years. Position Overview: The assistant will aid in the management of a busy admissions office, answering phones, interacting with prospective families, filing, and entering data on prospective students into the admissions database. The assistant will also be trained to help facilitate testing, grade applicant essays, and conduct applicant interviews. The assistant will work 35 hours a week (9-5 with a one hour lunch break each day), and will also be expected to work a handful of Saturdays or Sundays throughout the fall, or to stay late some weeknights. Any hours outside of 9 a.m. - 5 p.m. will be comped and the assistant will be able to take off the same number of hours the week or two immediately following their overtime work (specific timing to be determined in conversation with the Director of Admissions). Interested candidates should submit a cover letter and a resume. Compensation: $17 per hour Start Date: October 2026 End Date: January 2027 Duration: October 2026 to January 2027 (this is the school year (SY) 26-27 admissions season) Location: Bard High School Early College Brooklyn located at 301 Vermont Street, Brooklyn, NY 11207 Qualifications The ideal candidate should thrive in a fast paced environment The ideal candidate is a detail-oriented and well-organized individual This position is great for a recent college graduate and/or someone with a flexible schedule and a strong interest in education. Application Instructions Please apply by clicking on the \"Apply Now” button found on the top right corner through the Interfolio job application link provided here: Use the Interfolio link provided to upload the following documents directly with Bard College: Letter of interest C.V. / resume Questions If you have a question about the BHSEC Brooklyn-centered position, please direct them to [email protected] .  Please include your name and “Admissions Support – Short-term (BHSEC Brooklyn” in the subject line of the email. Bard High School Early College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from those who contribute to our diversity. Women and members of under-represented groups are strongly encouraged to apply Bard College is AA/EOE & welcomes applications from individuals who contribute to its diversity AA/EOE Human Resources Quick Links ADP Workforce Now Payroll Website Office of Title IX and Nondiscrimination Dispute Resolution & Peace Building Office Office of the Dean of the College Contact Us Bard College Office of Human Resources Mailing Address: PO Box 5000, (Street Address: 30 Campus Road) Annandale-on-Hudson, NY 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-7428 or Fax: 845-758-7826 Email: [email protected] We are open Monday through Friday, 9am - 5pm Equal Opportunity Employer Equal Opportunity Employer × Equal Opportunity Employer Bard College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities. 30 Campus Road, PO Box 5000 Annandale-on-Hudson, New York 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-6822 Admission Email: [email protected] Bard has a long history of creating inclusive environments for all races, creeds, ethnicities, and genders. We will continue to monitor and adhere to all Federal and New York State laws and guidance. Information For Prospective Students Current Employees Alumni/ae Families ©2026 Bard College Quick Links Employment Travel to Bard Search Support Bard Bard IT Policies + Security Bard Privacy Notice"
    },
    "https://www.bard.edu/humanresources/descriptions/?id=6927436": {
      "title": "Learning Center Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Opportunities at Bard College Skip to main content. Bard Bard Menu Academics sub-menu Academics Programs and Divisions Structure of the Curriculum Courses Requirements Academic Calendar College Catalogue Faculty Bard Abroad Bard NYC Dual-Degree Programs Bard Conservatory of Music Other Study Opportunities Graduate Programs Early Colleges Admission sub-menu Admission Applying Financial Aid Tuition + Payment Campus Tours Meet Our Students + Alumni/ae For Families / Familias Join Our Mailing List Contact Us Campus Life sub-menu Campus Life Living on Campus: Housing + Dining Campus Services + Resources Campus Activities New Students Visiting + Transportation Athletics + Recreation Montgomery Place Campus Civic Engagement sub-menu Civic Engagement Bard CCE Engaged Learning Student Leadership Grow Your Network About CCE Our Partners Get Involved Newsroom sub-menu News + Events Newsroom Events Calendar Press Releases Office of Communications Commencement Weekend Alumni/ae Reunion Family and Alumni/ae Weekend Fisher Center + SummerScape Athletic Events About Bard sub-menu About About Bard: Administration Bard History Campus Tours Mission Statement Love of Learning Visiting Bard Employment Support Bard Global Higher Education Alliance for the 21st Century Bard Abroad The Bard Network Inclusive Excellence Sustainability Title IX and Nondiscrimination Inside Bard Dean of the College Policy Library Giving Search Search Bard Employment Opportunities View All Opportunities HR Menu HR Menu Info sub-menu Information For: Applicants Current Employees New Employees Info sub-menu Bard Benefits Current Offerings TIAA Retirement Plan Emeritus Faculty Benefits Benefits Portal Info sub-menu Employee Resources Forms + Handbooks Training + Policies Wellness Affinity + Working Groups COVID-19 Workplace Rights Home Bard High School Early College Brooklyn Learning Center Coordinator Apply Here: https://apply.interfolio.com/160823 About the Bard Early Colleges The Bard Early Colleges (BEC) are founded on the belief that, for many young people, college can and should start at an earlier age. Acting on this belief, Bard Early College enables students to begin serious college study in place of the traditional 11th and 12th grades, at no cost to students or families. The Bard Early Colleges offer a unique home for young people’s intellectual ambition: as both tuition-free, branch campuses of Bard College and public high schools, they award a high school diploma and a Bard College Associate in Arts degree (and 60 transferable credits) by the end of the 12th grade. Students are taught by Bard College faculty in undergraduate, seminar classes, all deeply rooted in the liberal arts and sciences, in Bard College’s commitment to excellence in teaching, and in Bard’s mission as a private college in the public interest. Now entering its third decade, the Bard Early College network enrolls over 3,300 young people in campuses in Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx, Manhattan, and Hudson, New York; Newark, New Jersey; New Orleans, Louisiana; Cleveland, Ohio; Baltimore, Maryland; and Washington, D.C. Bard High School Early College (BHSEC) Brooklyn, a partnership between Bard College and the New York City Department of Education, invites applications for a Learning Center Coordinator to join our campus community! Position Duties The Learning Center Coordinator's responsibilities will include working with students individually, tutoring them in writing, math, and/or science, depending on the Coordinator’s specialization; working closely with other student support staff and faculty to monitor and support students who are struggling; teaching Advisory and related co-curricular courses; supervising study periods and substituting; being available to students for support of all kinds; and providing additional administrative support, as needed. Location: Bard High School Early College (BHSEC) Brooklyn, 301 Vermont Street, Brooklyn, NY 11207 Start Date: September or October 2026 Duration: Full-time, ongoing Compensation: The salary range for this position is $50,000 - $55,000 per year We are pleased to offer our full-time employees an excellent benefit package. Qualifications The Learning Center Coordinator's qualifications include: B.A. or M.A. in a liberal arts and sciences discipline  (corresponding to a field of  study within the Bard Early College curriculum); interest in engaging and challenging younger students with diverse racial backgrounds, economic backgrounds, and a variety of approaches to learning and/or needs for learning supports; peer tutoring experience; strong organizational and communication skills. A demonstrated ability to effectively communicate with adolescents; and experience with early college programs strongly preferred. Application Instructions Please apply directly with Bard College / Bard Early Colleges.  Do this by clicking on the “Apply Now” button found through the Interfolio job application link provided here: https://apply.interfolio.com/160823 Use the Interfolio link provided to upload the following documents directly with Bard College: letter of interest curriculum vitae / resume a list of 3 references, including their complete contact information Review of applications begins immediately and will proceed until the position is filled. Questions: If you have inquiries about the position, please contact Assistant Principal, Shawn Steele at [email protected] .  Please include the subject \"Question about the Learning Center Coordinator Position\" in your email. Bard High School Early College is an equal opportunity employer and we welcome applications from those who contribute to our diversity. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard High School Early College is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities. Visit https://www.bard.edu/earlycollege/about/ for more information on our schools. AA/EOE Human Resources Quick Links ADP Workforce Now Payroll Website Office of Title IX and Nondiscrimination Dispute Resolution & Peace Building Office Office of the Dean of the College Contact Us Bard College Office of Human Resources Mailing Address: PO Box 5000, (Street Address: 30 Campus Road) Annandale-on-Hudson, NY 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-7428 or Fax: 845-758-7826 Email: [email protected] We are open Monday through Friday, 9am - 5pm Equal Opportunity Employer Equal Opportunity Employer × Equal Opportunity Employer Bard College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities. 30 Campus Road, PO Box 5000 Annandale-on-Hudson, New York 12504-5000 Phone: 845-758-6822 Admission Email: [email protected] Bard has a long history of creating inclusive environments for all races, creeds, ethnicities, and genders. We will continue to monitor and adhere to all Federal and New York State laws and guidance. Information For Prospective Students Current Employees Alumni/ae Families ©2026 Bard College Quick Links Employment Travel to Bard Search Support Bard Bard IT Policies + Security Bard Privacy Notice"
